  "body": "## Result\n\nThis package gives an exact minimum of four paid reflection calls for\n`diag([st],[ts],[e])` in the formal group algebra of the order-10 dihedral\ngroup `D10=<s,t | s^2=t^2=e,(st)^5=e>`, on three arbitrary dirty scalar\nregisters and with paid labels restricted to `{s,t}`.\n\nThe proposed shared `s,t,s` schedule does not work. The verifier exhausts all\nrank-one idempotent choices in `M3(F2)` and all ordered label words through\nlength three: 1, 56, 3,136 and 175,616 cases by length, with zero exact\nendpoints. A direct four-call word attains the target. A second engine builds\nthe group by permutations of the pentagon and uses row-mask outer products;\nit independently covers the same domain with distinct per-level hashes.\n\nThis tests the finite torsion boundary left by PR #1911's `D_infinity`\nreflection theorem. It does not extend that theorem to other quotients, groups,\nregister counts or alphabets.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/d10-reflection-sharing-seeda3def8/verify.py\npython3 -I -B research/d10-reflection-sharing-seeda3def8/independent.py\npython3 -I -O -B research/d10-reflection-sharing-seeda3def8/test_package.py\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/d10-reflection-sharing-seeda3def8 --check-only\nmake selected-record-check\n```\n\nBoth mathematical replays and the optimized controls passed locally under\nCPython 3.14.7; metadata and source pins passed; `make selected-record-check`\npassed. This machine has no Python 3.12 interpreter, so the registered Python\n3.12 replay is left to the repository workflow. The research baseline also\npassed as `PASS_RESEARCH_BASELINE_BINDINGS_ONLY` earlier in this cycle.\n\n## Pins, limits and attribution\n\nBase: `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`. Selected-result SHA-256:\n`10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`.\nThe task seed is `a3def8e7b944810f5d933bfa65cba990`; the exact search certificate,\nsource manifest, task card and all source hashes are in the package.\n\nThe result is a scoped finite-group obstruction only. No supplier/compiler,\nwhole-interface cost, physical hosting, precision, recursive moment, new\n`kappa` or selected-frontier change is claimed. The selected conditional\n`kappa` remains `836330098538459/500000000000000000`.\n\nPR #1911 (infinite dihedral reflection bills), PR #1821 (D16 central pair),\nPR #1573 (D8 central target), and PR #1870 (S3 target pairs) are credited and\npinned in `SOURCES.json`. New open PR #1941 (head\n`5938ce3e91bbb8b5c2227af7976d444b2fbac7d4`), claimed in Discussion #1929\ncomment 18925900, proves tariffs for every even rotation order and expressly\nleaves odd periods out. This package treats odd rotation order five and the\ninverse-rotation pair. The final overlap refresh at 2026-10-14 14:56:57 UTC\ncovered 601 open PRs and 575 Discussions with complete pagination and no\nwarnings; no D10 target claim was found. Prepared with\nsubstantial OpenAI Codex assistance. No independent human review is claimed.\n",
